    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0567" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2756</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Berlin</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-07-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 26, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 27, 11.10 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>245. <hi rendition="#italic">Imperial Gazette</hi> published last evening
                    amendment to prize ordinance of September 30, 1909, which went into effect July
                    22 last. New regulations which are officially stated nature reprisal for
                    position Great Britain and Allies on London Declaration, contain new lists
                    absolute and relative contraband, new free list, and commentaries showing German
                    position on points of controversy. Official copies amendment have been forwarded
                    Department in to-day’s mail.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d371-f1"/> Lists are long but
                    will be cabled if desired.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
